  text: "THE $35K MOTION WEBSITE STACK IS NOT A STUDIO ANYMORE. IT IS HIGGSFIELD PLUS\
    \ CLAUDE CODE SKILLS.\n\nMost people still think premium motion sites require\
    \ a design team, an animation specialist, and a long handoff between Figma, video,\
    \ and front-end code. This stack turns that into a repo-level workflow.\n\nclaudedesignskills\
    \ gives Claude Code the front-end brain: Three.js, GSAP, React Three Fiber, Motion,\
    \ Babylon, scroll patterns, and interactive experience logic.  \nhttps://t.co/0RViGWnA11\n\
    \ngsap-skills keeps the animation layer from hallucinating. ScrollTrigger, timelines,\
    \ React patterns, plugins, and performance rules become part of the agent’s working\
    \ memory.  \nhttps://t.co/guuRC4pGi5\n\nThe polish comes from motion-dev-animations-skill:\
    \ hero fade-ups, scroll reveals, parallax, magnetic buttons, reduced-motion support,\
    \ and GPU-safe animation defaults.  \nhttps://t.co/hujGQwR7up\n\nThe detail most\
    \ people miss: Higgsfield is the asset layer. higgsfield-skill plugs Claude Code\
    \ into models like Seedance, Sora, Veo, Kling, Soul, and Cinema.  \nhttps://t.co/lmiUEAoMrV\n\
    \nclaude-seedance-skill turns prompts into hero and background video assets, then\
    \ feeds them straight into the scroll site pipeline.  \nhttps://t.co/o7g5upMe3V\n\
    \nThat is the full pipeline. Higgsfield generates the cinematic raw material,\
    \ Seedance renders the motion, and Claude Code assembles the site with GSAP, https://t.co/NMEYeU8oNO,\
    \ and design-grade front-end skills.\n\nMost people are still asking Claude to\
    \ write components. A few are giving it the skills, assets, animation rules, and\
    \ visual pipeline to ship something that looks like an agency billed five figures\
    \ for it."
