- id: '2080382123169464577'
  text: 'Rebuild the website shown in the attached video, as closely as possible.
    It''s a dark, cinematic, scroll-driven product-reveal page for a high-tech aircraft
    ("GEODE CORE"), with a real-time interactive 3D model. Recreate the look, layout,
    motion, and interactions faithfully.


    MATCH THIS EXACTLY:

    - Aesthetic: near-black background (#0A0A0B), off-white text, ONE accent — hot
    orange engine glow (#FF6A00). Hairline grey UI lines, heavy black negative space.

    - Type: technical MONOSPACE for labels/stats + heavy CONDENSED display sans for
    the giant headlines. UPPERCASE, wide tracking. Micro-labels in "// " format (e.g.
    "AIRFRAME // DUAL SYSTEM", "PROPULSION // CLASSIFIED", "EXPLORE // INTERACTIVE").

    - Nav: left "◈ GEODE CORE", center links (AIRFRAME · PROPULSION · DEPLOYMENT),
    right icons + ghost "BRIEFING" and solid white "ACQUIRE" buttons.

    - Sections (one persistent 3D model transforms between them): HERO "DUAL SYSTEM
    AIRFRAME" + stats (18.4m wingspan, 72,000ft ceiling) → PROPULSION "ZERO THERMAL
    SIGNATURE" + stats (Mach 3.2, 0.0% signature, Level 5) → INTERACTIVE "DRAG TO
    EXPLORE" → ACQUIRE CTA.

    - 3D model: a quad-rotor drone stacked above a delta-wing stealth jet with a glowing
    orange engine core.

    - Bottom: section-progress rail + live scroll percentage. Small hints "↻ DRAG
    TO ROTATE / ⌕ SCROLL TO ZOOM / RESET VIEW".


    BEHAVIOR TO REPRODUCE:

    - Scroll drives the camera and the model — it rotates, the drone/jet separate
    and converge (exploded view), reframing per section, scrubbed to scroll progress.

    - In the INTERACTIVE section, hand control to the user: drag to rotate 360°, scroll
    to zoom, RESET VIEW button. Elsewhere the camera is scripted.

    - Headlines glitch/scramble in on section enter; stat numbers count up; engine
    ring glows with bloom and pulses; smooth eased camera, no snapping.


    STACK: Next.js + TypeScript + Tailwind, React Three Fiber (Three.js) + drei (OrbitControls,
    GLTF Draco), GSAP ScrollTrigger + Lenis, light postprocessing (bloom on the orange
    glow, vignette, faint grain). 60fps, responsive, prefers-reduced-motion fallback.


    I''ll supply the 3D model as a GLTF — scaffold everything around a placeholder
    /public/model.glb (a stacked drone+jet) and make it easy to swap in. Build the
    full working site: nav → hero → propulsion → interactive → acquire, with the persistent
    scroll-driven + draggable model and the spec-sheet HUD.'
